   "text": "I read the molecule as a macrocycle built from Dab, Lys, and N-methyl-Trp residues, closed through a pyridyl-thio-aryl linker.\n\n**Residues and linker**\n- **Dab:** H2N\u2011CH2CH2\u2011CH(\u03b1\u2011C) with the \u03b1\u2011NH linked through a CH2 to C3 of the pyridine. Its C=O is amide-bonded to the Lys NH.\n- **Lys:** The side chain is (CH2)4NH2. Its C=O is bonded to the N\u2011methyl nitrogen of Trp.\n- **N\u2011Me\u2011Trp:** The side chain is CH2\u2011indol\u20113\u2011yl. Its C=O is bonded to an NH, which connects through a CH2 to the central benzene ring.\n- **Central benzene ring:** Going round the ring, the substituents are S (to pyridine C2), then CH2NH, then the aryl group, then two CH, then Cl. The Cl-bearing carbon sits next to the S-bearing carbon.\n- **Aryl group:** A 4-carboxy-3-hydroxyphenyl, i.e. the salicylic acid part.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nThe three \u03b1\u2011carbons carry wedges. Working out CIP priorities from the drawing, all three come out S, the L-configuration. I then converted this to SMILES `@`/`@@` using the neighbour order in the string.\n\n**Ring-closure digits**\nThe Trp indole uses digits 4 and 5 so they do not clash with the benzene ring that is still open at that point.\n\nSMILES: NCC[C@@H]1NCc2cccnc2Sc2c(Cl)ccc(-c3ccc(C(=O)O)c(O)c3)c2CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc4c[nH]c5ccccc45)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC1=O"
